From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn-patches <tyn-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:50:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: STEINS;GATE 0 instruction set (InstructionSet::SG0)

STEINS;GATE 0 (Steam, 2018) runs the STEINS;GATE (Steam) dialect of the SC3
VM: the opcode tables of its Game.exe (system 0xdcc198, graph 0xdcbfb0, user 1
0xdcc320) have the same operand shapes except for a few groups.
InstructionSet::SG0 starts from the SGHD tables (Configure_SG0 in
opcodetables_sg0.h) and overrides:

- 00:53..00:59 (unused by S;G): 00:53 read and ignored, CallIfFlag,
  JumpFarIfFlag, CallFarIfFlag, ReturnIfFlag, mouse on jump (0x47f770:
  rectangles in 1280x720 units, button masks), keyboard on jump (0x47f980:
  KBcustom or key codes, "is down" / "went down").
- 10:37 / 10:38 operand shapes of the RINE / phone group (0x482df0,
  0x4831a0), read and skipped for now.

Everywhere the engine treats SGHD specially, SG0 follows it (backgrounds and
captures tint, movie priority 10000, backlog by flick or wheel, SystemMes id
byte, MSinit ranges and movie channels, backlog show / hide, Sel save point,
NameID name plates, title menu, LoadSystemData without a save file). Press
start is taken at any time in title mode 1 (Game.exe 0x45c321), not only once
SW_TITLEDISPCT reaches 60.

TYN only (new game generation, no upstream support yet).

Verified on MuMu (Android 15 x86_64 emulator, not a real device), sg0-pc
(Steam data, Chinese scripts): startup movies, title, new game, prologue and
chapter 1 to SG0_B01_12 at x64 with the debug mode, world line change and
chapter title movies, NVL pages. RINE / phone screens not implemented.

